 are only read from `~/.grok/config.toml`.\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2016:MCP tools are namespaced with the server name:\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2026:[mcp_servers.filesystem]\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2034:[mcp_servers.github]\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2043:[mcp_servers.postgres]\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2051:[mcp_servers.my-tools]\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2052:command = \"/usr/local/bin/my-mcp-server\"\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2053:args = [\"--config\", \"/etc/my-mcp.json\"]\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2061:[mcp_servers.my-http-mcp]\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2062:url = \"http://localhost:5000/api/mcp\"\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2066:### Available MCP Servers\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2068:See the [MCP Server Registry](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers) for community servers:\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2301:- **Plugins** — discovered plugins with what each provides (skills, agents, hooks, MCPs)\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2302:- **MCP Servers** — from `config.toml`, plugins, `~/.claude.json`, and `.mcp.json`\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2307:Plugin-provided components appear in their respective sections with a `[plugin: name]` tag, so you can see at a glance where each skill, MCP server, or agent originates.\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2324:| **MCP servers**   | `~/.claude.json`, `.mcp.json`                        | Loaded alongside `config.toml`   |\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2330:Claude Code plugins can provide skills (`skills/`), commands (`commands/`), agents (`agents/`), hooks (`hooks/hooks.json`), MCP servers (`.mcp.json`), and LSP servers (`.lsp.json`). All component types are discovered and used by Grok at runtime.\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2353:| `search_tool`    | Discover available integration tools (MCP)                     |\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2449:  mcpServers: [],\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2456:  mcpServers: [],\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2475:| `.grok/config.toml`   | Project-scoped config (MCP servers)                 |\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2483:| `~/.claude.json`      | MCP servers (Claude Code compat)                    |\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2484:| `.mcp.json`           | Project-scoped MCP servers (Claude Code compat)     |\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2628:### MCP server not starting\n/home/debian19y/.grok/README.md:2635:[mcp_servers.filesystem]\n/home/debian19y/.grok/docs/user-guide/02-authentication.md:19:Tokens in `~/.grok/auth.json` (and MCP OAuth tokens in `~/.grok/mcp_credentials.json`) are written with owner-only permissions (`0600` on Unix). Anyone with filesystem access to those paths can use the credentials, so:\n"}
